    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dc2\u0dcf\u0dab\u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dca\u200d\u0db4\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dd9\u0dcf\u0dab\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0db8\u0dca \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bc6\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbf\u0baf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bc6\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b9c\u0baa\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bc6\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0b87\u0bc6\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bc6\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Shanakiyan Rajaputhiran Rasamanickam) Hon. Speaker, I would like to raise the following Question.\n\nSir, I raise this Question having understood that in the past, when the previous Government was there, there was a loan allocated for the development of the port. Later, after this Government came in, as I understand, it was converted into a grant. Now, two years down the road, we have not had enough progress.\n\nAlso, Sir, I would like omit my first question from the set of questions under this and start with the second question because I have come to understand that the matters raised in the first question had been addressed since I submitted the Question. I spoke to the Hon.\n\n1397 1398\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dad\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc3\u0da2\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dca \u0dba\u0dda\u0db8\u0daf\u0dcf\u0dc3 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0dc3\u0dd0\u0dca \u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6 11\n\nMinister also and I had been told that there was a joint meeting held between the delegation from the Indian side and the Government side and that certain progress has been made on that matter. So, I would like to omit the first question because I was told that the KKS Port project is now moving in the right direction. Therefore, I would like to omit the first question and start off with the second one.\n\n2. The Hon. Bimal Rathnayake has stated that the Government has the final say on these projects that I mentioned and the economic development projects must benefit the people. This is a matter for the Ministry of Ports and Civil Aviation. As he is not the Minister in charge of ports or civil aviation, I would like to know in what official capacity were these statements made and do they represent the Government policy?"
  },
