    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dbd \u0db1 \u0dc4\u0d9a\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dca \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bc6\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0ba3\u0bbf \u0bc6\u0b8a\u0baa\u0bcd \u0bb9\u0b95\u0bc0\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Rauff Hakeem, Attorney-at-Law) This request had been made during the peacetime and now, unfortunately, our Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism is taking an inordinate time to comply with this simple request of replacing three sailors. The original request was for 13 sailors to be replaced, but the Ministry of Defence has permitted only three to be replaced. So, with the anxious parents of these young sailors waiting for their return home, would the Government kindly consider this request without any further delay and avoid an unnecessary diplomatic confrontation with our friendly nation, Iran?\n\n\u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dd9\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bc6\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0db4\u0dd2\u0dc5\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dbb \u0dbd\u0db6\u0dcf \u0daf\u0dd3\u0db8, \u0d9c\u0dad\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dda \u0dba\u0dc4\u0dca\u0db8\u0da0\u0dda\u0dbb \u0dd2\u0dba\u0dba\u0dba \u0da2\u0dba \u0d85\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf\u0db4\n\nSri Lanka has approached this exceptional situation throughout with humanitarian consideration, responsibility and constructive diplomatic engagement while acting in accordance with our established procedures and national responsibilities. From the outset, the Government has given due attention to the safety, welfare and the dignity of the Iranian personnel concerned.\n\nSri Lanka facilitated the dignified repatriation of the remains of the deceased personnel and has also facilitated the repatriation of 238 Iranian sailors to Iran. These arrangements were carried out through close coordination among the relevant Sri Lankan authorities and in communication with the Iranian side, reflecting Sri Lanka\u2019s long-standing approach of extending humanitarian assistance where circumstances require it.\n\nThe Government continues to address the remaining matters through the appropriate diplomatic, defence and administrative channels with due regard to the humanitarian considerations involved and Sri Lanka\u2019s sovereignty, security and international responsibilities."
  },
